course: dictionary
lesson: 754
title: Bawl and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bawl is a verb, so it is something a person or animal does. It means to make a very loud noise, usually with the voice.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. «The baby bawled all night» pictures a child crying very loudly. «The coach bawled instructions across the pitch» pictures someone shouting roughly.
explain: In Alice in Wonderland, the Queen «bawled out» at the Hatter. The bracket that follows, (shouted), is the author's clue. Bawl out here means shout.
explain: Sometimes bawl out means to tell someone off angrily, as in «The teacher bawled him out for being late.» Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Bawl means to cry very loudly, like a baby.
fact: Bawl also means to shout loudly and roughly.
fact: «Bawl someone out» is informal and means to tell them off angrily.
fact: The forms of bawl are bawls, bawled and bawling.
fact: «Bawled» shows that the noise happened in the past.
exercise: «The baby bawled all through the night.» What does bawled mean here? | To laugh with joy | To whisper softly | To sleep quietly | *To cry very loudly
exercise: «The Queen bawled out, "He's murdering the time!"» What does bawled out mean in this sentence? | Fell asleep | *Shouted | Sang sweetly | Whispered
exercise: «Mr Patel bawled out the boy for breaking the window.» What does bawl out mean here? | Gave him a present | Cried with him | Thanked him warmly | *Told him off angrily
test: The coach bawls instructions across the field. What does bawls mean? | Falls over | *Shouts loudly and roughly | Whispers gently | Sings a song
test: Which phrase means to tell someone off angrily? | Ask someone to sit down | *Bawl someone out | Give someone a hug | Cheer someone up
exam: Which sentence uses bawl to mean cry very loudly? | The teacher bawled out the class. | Grandma sang a lullaby. | *The baby bawled all night. | The dog wagged its tail happily.
